{"name":"Greenish Beige","hex":"#c9d179","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"greenish","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Somewhat green in color."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/greenish"},{"term":"beige","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A colour, variously defined from a pale brown, to a yellow greyish off-white.","Debeige; a kind of woollen or mixed dress goods."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a slightly yellowish gray colour, as that of unbleached wool.","Comfortably dull and unadventurous, in a way that suggests middle-class suburbia."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/beige"}],"entries":[{"title":"Beige","blocks":[{"text":"Beige is variously described as a pale sandy fawn color, a grayish tan, a light-grayish yellowish brown, or a pale to grayish yellow. It takes its name from French, where the word originally meant natural wool that has been neither bleached nor dyed, hence also the color of natural wool."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Saint_Anthony_church_in_Chamboret_07.jpg/330px-Saint_Anthony_church_in_Chamboret_07.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beige","wikidata":"Q843607"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/41/Klaus-J%C3%BCrgen_Bauer.jpg/500px-Klaus-J%C3%BCrgen_Bauer.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/41/Klaus-J%C3%BCrgen_Bauer.jpg/500px-Klaus-J%C3%BCrgen_Bauer.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKlaus-J%C3%BCrgen_Bauer.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a3/1981_AMC_Concord_4-door_beige_PAfr.jpg/500px-1981_AMC_Concord_4-door_beige_PAfr.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_cam